<section id="as1_S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="as1_S1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.1 </span>Proof of Theorem 1</h3>

<div id="as1_S1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the proof of Theorem 1 (asymptotic properties of CALM with zero-shot learning) from the main paper. Following standard arguments for analyzing estimators with estimated nuisance functions, the proof is divided into two parts. In the first part, we establish the asymptotic properties of the <em id="as1_S1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">oracle</em> CALM estimator, which is defined using the true nuisance functions <math id="as1_S1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="as1_S1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\dagger}_{t}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\dagger}_{t}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="as1_S1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{t}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{t}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> rather than their estimates:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\varphi_{t}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\varphi_{t}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varphi_{t}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varphi_{t}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}Y_{i}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}+\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)\bigg(\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)+\omega_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\left(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}Y_{i}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}+\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)\bigg(\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)+\omega_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\left(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We first state the following lemma on the asymptotic behavior of <math id="as1_S1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="as1_Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="as1_Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Asymptotic properties of the oracle CALM estimator)<span id="as1_Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions 1-2, the oracle CALM estimator is a consistent and asymptotically normal estimator of <math id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, we have <math id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}\xrightarrow{p}\mu_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}\xrightarrow{p}\mu_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{n}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}-\mu_{t}\right)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}\left(0,\mathsf{V}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{n}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}-\mu_{t}\right)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}\left(0,\mathsf{V}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the asymptotic variance is given by:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t}\right)^{2}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)}{e_{t}(X)}\left(1-(1-e_{t}(X))\rho_{t}^{2}(X)\right)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t}\right)^{2}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)}{e_{t}(X)}\left(1-(1-e_{t}(X))\rho_{t}^{2}(X)\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <math id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}(x)=\mathbb{C}\text{orr}(Y(t),Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X=x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">orr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}(x)=\mathbb{C}\text{orr}(Y(t),Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X=x)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the conditional correlation between the true potential outcome and the LLM-based prediction. For covariate values <math id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X=x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X=x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="as1_Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math> by convention.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the second part, we show that under Assumption 3, the estimation error arising from cross-fitted nuisance functions is asymptotically negligible relative to the oracle CALM estimator. This is formalized in the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="as1_Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="as1_Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Asymptotic equivalence to oracle)<span id="as1_Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions 1–3, the proposed CALM estimator <math id="as1_Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Section 2.1) is asymptotically equivalent to the oracle CALM estimator <math id="as1_Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}</annotation></semantics></math>, in the sense that</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}\big)=o_{p}(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}\big)=o_{p}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma 2 implies that
<math id="as1_S1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}-\mu_{t}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}-\mu_{t}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
shares the same asymptotic distribution as
<math id="as1_S1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}-\mu_{t}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}-\mu_{t}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>,
thereby completing the proof of Theorem 1.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="as1_S1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.2 </span>Proof of Lemma 1</h3>

<div id="as1_S1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="as1_S1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove the result in two steps: (i) consistency and asymptotic normality, and (ii) asymptotic variance computation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Consistency and asymptotic normality.</span>
For any integrable function <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(X,Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(X,Z)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(1-\frac{1\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\right)h(X,Z)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(1-\frac{1\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\right)h(X,Z)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[\left.\left(1-\frac{1\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\right)h(X,Z)\right\rvert\,X,Z\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">|</mo></mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[\left.\left(1-\frac{1\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\right)h(X,Z)\right\rvert\,X,Z\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[h(X,Z)\left(1-\frac{\mathbb{E}[1\{T=t\}\mid X,Z]}{e_{t}(X)}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[h(X,Z)\left(1-\frac{\mathbb{E}[1\{T=t\}\mid X,Z]}{e_{t}(X)}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the last equality uses Assumption 1 that <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[1\{T=t\}\mid X,Z]=E[1\{T=t\}\mid X]=e_{t}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[1\{T=t\}\mid X,Z]=E[1\{T=t\}\mid X]=e_{t}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall from the main paper that the LLM-based zero-shot prediction <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\dagger}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\dagger}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as function of the query covariates <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Z)</annotation></semantics></math> and the treatment arm <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, namely <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}\big((X,Z),t\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}\big((X,Z),t\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the pre-trained parameters of the LLM. Hence, <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}(X)+\omega_{t}(X)(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\mu^{\dagger}_{t}(X))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}(X)+\omega_{t}(X)(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\mu^{\dagger}_{t}(X))</annotation></semantics></math> is a function with respect to <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Z)</annotation></semantics></math>. The above argument then implies:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\varphi_{t}(Y,T,X,Y^{\dagger}(t))]=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}Y}{e_{t}(X)}\bigg]=\mathbb{E}[Y(t)]=\mu_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\varphi_{t}(Y,T,X,Y^{\dagger}(t))]=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}Y}{e_{t}(X)}\bigg]=\mathbb{E}[Y(t)]=\mu_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{t}(Y,T,X,Y^{\dagger}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{t}(Y,T,X,Y^{\dagger}(t))</annotation></semantics></math> is an unbiased estimating function for <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Assumptions 2, the sequence <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\varphi_{t}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\varphi_{t}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is i.i.d. with finite variance. Therefore, the standard Law of Large Numbers (LLN) and Central Limit Theorem (CLT) yield</p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}\xrightarrow{p}\mu_{t},\quad\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}-\mu_{t}\big)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\mathbb{V}\text{ar}(\varphi_{t})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>ar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}\xrightarrow{p}\mu_{t},\quad\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}-\mu_{t}\big)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\mathbb{V}\text{ar}(\varphi_{t})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Asymptotic variance computation.</span> We now show the detailed computation of the asymptotic variance <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition,</p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex11X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex11X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex11X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[(\varphi_{t}(Y,T,X,Y^{\dagger}(t))-\mu_{t})^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[(\varphi_{t}(Y,T,X,Y^{\dagger}(t))-\mu_{t})^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex11Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex11Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex11Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left\{\left[\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t}+\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\left(Y-\mu_{t}(X)\right)+\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\right)\omega_{t}(X)\left(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(X)\right)\right]^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left\{\left[\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t}+\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\left(Y-\mu_{t}(X)\right)+\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\right)\omega_{t}(X)\left(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(X)\right)\right]^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex11Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex11Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex11Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t}\right)^{2}\right]+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))^{2}\Bigr]}_{\text{(I)}}+2\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\Bigl[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})\cdot\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))\Bigr]}_{\text{(II)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>(I)</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>(II)</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t}\right)^{2}\right]+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))^{2}\Bigr]}_{\text{(I)}}+2\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\Bigl[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})\cdot\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))\Bigr]}_{\text{(II)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex12X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex12X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex12X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\left(Y-\mu_{t}(X)\right)+\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\right)\omega_{t}(X)\left(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(X)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\left(Y-\mu_{t}(X)\right)+\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\right)\omega_{t}(X)\left(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(X)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">A direct variance–covariance expansion yields</p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{(I)}=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\frac{1}{e_{t}(X)}\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)+\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}\Big(\omega_{t}^{2}(X)\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X)-2\,\omega_{t}(X)\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(Y(t),Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X)\Big)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>(I)</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{(I)}=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\frac{1}{e_{t}(X)}\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)+\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}\Big(\omega_{t}^{2}(X)\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X)-2\,\omega_{t}(X)\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(Y(t),Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X)\Big)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{(II)}=\mathbb{E}\!\Big[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})\cdot\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))\mid X]\Big]=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>(II)</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{(II)}=\mathbb{E}\!\Big[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})\cdot\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))\mid X]\Big]=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">since <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))\mid X]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))\mid X]=0</annotation></semantics></math> by construction. Then, substituting (I) and (II) gives</p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t})=\mathbb{E}\!\left[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)+\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}\,\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\!\big(Y(t)-\omega_{t}(X)Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X\big)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.838em;" width="0.838em"><mi>ar</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t})=\mathbb{E}\!\left[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)+\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}\,\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\!\big(Y(t)-\omega_{t}(X)Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X\big)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p">To minimize the asymptotic variance, recall from Step 3 of the main paper that the heterogeneous calibration function is chosen as</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\omega_{t}(x)=\frac{\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}\left(Y,Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid T=t,X=x\right)}{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\left(Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid T=t,X=x\right)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>ov</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\omega_{t}(x)=\frac{\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}\left(Y,Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid T=t,X=x\right)}{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\left(Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid T=t,X=x\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.7" class="ltx_p">whenever <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X=x)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X=x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. If instead <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X=x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X=x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\!\big(Y(t)-\omega_{t}(X)Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X\big)=\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\!\big(Y(t)\mid X\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.838em;" width="0.838em"><mi>ar</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.838em;" width="0.838em"><mi>ar</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\!\big(Y(t)-\omega_{t}(X)Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X\big)=\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\!\big(Y(t)\mid X\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
for any choice of <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{t}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{t}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the definition of <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}=\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t})=\mathbb{E}\!\left[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)}{e_{t}(X)}\Big(1-(1-e_{t}(X))\rho_{t}^{2}(X)\Big)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}=\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t})=\mathbb{E}\!\left[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)}{e_{t}(X)}\Big(1-(1-e_{t}(X))\rho_{t}^{2}(X)\Big)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.8" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof of Lemma 1. In the special case where <math id="as1_S1.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{t}(x)\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{t}(x)\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., no information is borrowed from the LLM-based prediction), the asymptotic variance degenerates to:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{t,\texttt{AIPW}}=\mathbb{E}\left[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)}{e_{t}(X)}\right]=\mathsf{V}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">AIPW</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{t,\texttt{AIPW}}=\mathbb{E}\left[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)}{e_{t}(X)}\right]=\mathsf{V}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="as1_S1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.3 </span>Proof of Lemma 2</h3>

<div id="as1_S1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="as1_S1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By random sample splitting (Step 1) and the i.i.d. data collection procedure (Assumption 2), it suffices to show that</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}\right)=o_{p}(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}\right)=o_{p}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">We first decompose the difference as</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex20X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{n}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}\right)=\frac{\sqrt{n}}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{1}\right|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{n}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}\right)=\frac{\sqrt{n}}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{1}\right|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex20X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Bigg\{\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Bigg\{\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex20Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex20Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\omega_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\left(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\omega_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\left(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex20Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex20Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\omega_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">†</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\omega_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex20Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex20Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\omega_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">†</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\omega_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">We now bound the remainder terms. For the first term, conditional on <math id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and the observed structured covariates <math id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, its variance is</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex21X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex21X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigg[\bigg(\frac{\sqrt{n}}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{1}\right|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\bigg)^{2}\bigg|\mathcal{I}_{2},\left\{X_{i}\right\}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigg[\bigg(\frac{\sqrt{n}}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{1}\right|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\bigg)^{2}\bigg|\mathcal{I}_{2},\left\{X_{i}\right\}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex21Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex21Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex21Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\bigg[\frac{\sqrt{n}}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{1}\right|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\bigg|I_{2},\left\{X_{i}\right\}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>ar</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\bigg[\frac{\sqrt{n}}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{1}\right|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\bigg|I_{2},\left\{X_{i}\right\}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex21Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex21Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex21Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{n}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{1}\right|^{2}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\mathbb{E}\bigg[\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)^{2}\bigg|I_{2},\left\{X_{i}\right\}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{n}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{1}\right|^{2}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\mathbb{E}\bigg[\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)^{2}\bigg|I_{2},\left\{X_{i}\right\}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex21Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex21Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex21Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{n}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{1}\right|^{2}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\frac{1-e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\leqslant C\cdot\frac{1}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{1}\right|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)^{2}=o_{p}\left(1\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{n}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{1}\right|^{2}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\frac{1-e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\leqslant C\cdot\frac{1}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{1}\right|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)^{2}=o_{p}\left(1\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the inequality uses Assumption 1 (propensity scores bounded away from <math id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>).
Since <math id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a consistent cross-fitted estimator (Assumption 3), the bound is <math id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. By Chebyshev’s inequality, the first remainder term is therefore <math id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> as well. Analogous arguments apply to the other remainder terms involving <math id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger\mathcal{I}_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">†</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger\mathcal{I}_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the final interaction term, the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality yields the same <math id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> rate. Putting everything together, we obtain <math id="as1_S1.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}\right)=o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}\right)=o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="as1_S1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.4 </span>Proof of Corollary 1</h3>

<div id="as1_S1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present the proof of Corollary 1 from the main paper. To begin, we define a deterministic function <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> that depends on the coarsened covariates <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathtt{C}}\in\{1,\ldots,M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathtt{C}}\in\{1,\ldots,M\}</annotation></semantics></math>. These coarsened covariates can be represented as the output of a deterministic mapping <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(X):\mathcal{X}\to\{1,\ldots,M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(X):\mathcal{X}\to\{1,\ldots,M\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed finite number that does not grow with the sample size <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})=\frac{\mathbb{E}\Big[\lambda_{t}(X)\left(Y(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}(X)\right)(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}^{\dagger}_{t}(X))\mid C(X)=x^{\mathtt{C}}\Big]}{\mathbb{E}\Big[\lambda_{t}(X)(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}^{\dagger}_{t}(X))^{2}\mid C(X)=x^{\mathtt{C}}\Big]}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})=\frac{\mathbb{E}\Big[\lambda_{t}(X)\left(Y(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}(X)\right)(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}^{\dagger}_{t}(X))\mid C(X)=x^{\mathtt{C}}\Big]}{\mathbb{E}\Big[\lambda_{t}(X)(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}^{\dagger}_{t}(X))^{2}\mid C(X)=x^{\mathtt{C}}\Big]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By defining the function in this way, we implicitly assume that the denominator is bounded away from <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathtt{C}}\in\{1,\ldots,M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathtt{C}}\in\{1,\ldots,M\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar to the proof of Theorem 1, we divide the proof of Corollary 1 into two parts. In the first part, we define the <span id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">oracle</span> CALM estimator with robust heterogeneous calibration weights as:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\varphi_{t,\mathtt{R}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\varphi_{t,\mathtt{R}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varphi_{t,\mathtt{R}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varphi_{t,\mathtt{R}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}Y_{i}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}+\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)\bigg(\widetilde{\mu}_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)+\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}\left(X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}}\right)\left(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\bigg)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}Y_{i}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}+\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)\bigg(\widetilde{\mu}_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)+\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}\left(X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}}\right)\left(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and the subscript <span id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">R</span> distinguishes this “robust” version of estimator from other parts. Analogous to Lemma 1, we now state the following results for <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="as1_Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="as1_Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Asymptotic properties of the oracle CALM estimator with robust calibration)<span id="as1_Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions 1-2, the oracle CALM estimator with robust heterogeneous calibration weights is a consistent and asymptotic normal estimator of <math id="as1_Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, we have <math id="as1_Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}\xrightarrow{p}\mu_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}\xrightarrow{p}\mu_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="as1_Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM}}-\mu_{t}\big)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\widetilde{\mathsf{V}}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖵</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM}}-\mu_{t}\big)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\widetilde{\mathsf{V}}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, where:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\mathsf{V}}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}=\mathbb{E}\!\left[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)+\sigma_{t}^{2}(X^{\mathrm{C}})\{1-\widetilde{\rho}_{t}^{2}(X^{\mathrm{C}})\}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖵</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\mathsf{V}}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}=\mathbb{E}\!\left[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)+\sigma_{t}^{2}(X^{\mathrm{C}})\{1-\widetilde{\rho}_{t}^{2}(X^{\mathrm{C}})\}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\rho}_{t}(x^{\mathrm{C}})=\frac{\mathbb{E}\!\left[\lambda_{t}(X)\{Y(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}(X)\}\{Y^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X)\}\,\middle|\,C(X)=x^{\mathrm{C}}\right]}{\sqrt{\sigma_{t}^{2}(x^{\mathrm{C}})\,\sigma_{t}^{\dagger 2}(x^{\mathrm{C}})}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">†</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\rho}_{t}(x^{\mathrm{C}})=\frac{\mathbb{E}\!\left[\lambda_{t}(X)\{Y(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}(X)\}\{Y^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X)\}\,\middle|\,C(X)=x^{\mathrm{C}}\right]}{\sqrt{\sigma_{t}^{2}(x^{\mathrm{C}})\,\sigma_{t}^{\dagger 2}(x^{\mathrm{C}})}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_Thmlemma3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><math id="as1_Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}(x^{\mathrm{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}(x^{\mathrm{C}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="as1_Thmlemma3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and <math id="as1_Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{\dagger 2}(x^{\mathrm{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">†</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{\dagger 2}(x^{\mathrm{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> are the weighted conditional mean squared deviations defined in Section 4.1 of the main paper.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="as1_S1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The consistency and asymptotic normality of <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}</annotation></semantics></math> follow directly from the proof of Lemma 1 (Section 1.2 in the Supplementary Materials), since <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(X^{\mathtt{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(X^{\mathtt{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> is a measurable function of <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be written rigorously as <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(C(X))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(C(X))</annotation></semantics></math> for the coarsening map <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>. For the asymptotic variance, by an argument parallel to that in the proof of Lemma 1, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t,\mathtt{R}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t,\mathtt{R}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\Big[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)+\lambda_{t}(X)\,\!\Big((Y(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}(X))-\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(C(X))\cdot(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}^{\dagger}_{t}(X))\Big)^{2}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\Big[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)+\lambda_{t}(X)\,\!\Big((Y(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}(X))-\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(C(X))\cdot(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}^{\dagger}_{t}(X))\Big)^{2}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Big[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Big[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}\Big[\mathbb{E}\Big[\lambda_{t}(X)\Big((Y(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}(X))-\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(C(X))(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}^{\dagger}_{t}(X))\Big)^{2}\Big|C(X)=X^{\mathtt{C}}\Big]\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}\Big[\mathbb{E}\Big[\lambda_{t}(X)\Big((Y(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}(X))-\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(C(X))(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}^{\dagger}_{t}(X))\Big)^{2}\Big|C(X)=X^{\mathtt{C}}\Big]\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the construction of <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(X^{\mathtt{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(X^{\mathtt{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> and the definition of <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}(x^{\mathrm{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}(x^{\mathrm{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{\dagger 2}(x^{\mathrm{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">†</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{\dagger 2}(x^{\mathrm{C}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the inner conditional expectation reduces to <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}(X^{\mathtt{C}})\{1-\widetilde{\rho}_{t}^{2}(X^{\mathtt{C}})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}(X^{\mathtt{C}})\{1-\widetilde{\rho}_{t}^{2}(X^{\mathtt{C}})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\mathsf{V}}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}=\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t,\mathtt{R}})=\mathbb{E}\!\left[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)+\sigma_{t}^{2}(X^{\mathrm{C}})\{1-\widetilde{\rho}_{t}^{2}(X^{\mathrm{C}})\}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖵</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\mathsf{V}}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}=\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t,\mathtt{R}})=\mathbb{E}\!\left[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t})^{2}+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)+\sigma_{t}^{2}(X^{\mathrm{C}})\{1-\widetilde{\rho}_{t}^{2}(X^{\mathrm{C}})\}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we show that the difference between <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM}}</annotation></semantics></math> is asymptotically negligible.</p>
</div>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="as1_Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="as1_Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions 1–2 and 4, we have
<math id="as1_Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}\big)=o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{R},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}\big)=o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="as1_S1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">As in Lemma 2, it suffices to show that the decomposition</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="as1_S1.E1X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.E1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}\big)=\frac{\sqrt{n}}{|\mathcal{I}_{1}|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}\Big)\Big\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}^{\mathcal{I}_{1}}\big)=\frac{\sqrt{n}}{|\mathcal{I}_{1}|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}\Big)\Big\{</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.E1X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}(X_{i})-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}(X_{i})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}(X_{i})-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}(X_{i})\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="as1_S1.E1Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.E1Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\big(\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{I_{2}}(X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}})-\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}})\big)(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\big(\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{I_{2}}(X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}})-\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}})\big)(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="as1_S1.E1Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.E1Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger I_{2}}(X_{i})-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})\big)\,\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">†</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger I_{2}}(X_{i})-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})\big)\,\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="as1_S1.E1Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.E1Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger I_{2}}(X_{i})-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})\big)\big(\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{I_{2}}(X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}})-\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}})\big)\Big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">†</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger I_{2}}(X_{i})-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})\big)\big(\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{I_{2}}(X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}})-\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}})\big)\Big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">consists of four remainder terms, each of which is <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. By the same argument as in Lemma 2, the first and third terms are <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> under Assumption 4. For the second term, write</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}=\frac{\sqrt{n}}{|\mathcal{I}_{1}|}\sum_{x^{\mathtt{C}}=1}^{M}\big(\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{I_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})-\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})\big)\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1},\,X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}}=x^{\mathtt{C}}}\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}\Big)(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}=\frac{\sqrt{n}}{|\mathcal{I}_{1}|}\sum_{x^{\mathtt{C}}=1}^{M}\big(\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{I_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})-\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})\big)\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1},\,X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}}=x^{\mathtt{C}}}\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}\Big)(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS4.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, we introduce the intermediate estimator <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> with the limiting (possibly misspecified) nuisance functions <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}_{t},\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}_{t},\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})=\frac{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}(t;x^{\mathtt{C}})}\lambda_{t}(X_{i})(Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}(X_{i}))(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i}))}{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}(t;x^{\mathtt{C}})}\lambda_{t}(X_{i})(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i}))^{2}},\quad\mathcal{I}_{1}(t;x^{\mathtt{C}})=\{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}:T_{i}=t,X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}}=x^{\mathtt{C}}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})=\frac{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}(t;x^{\mathtt{C}})}\lambda_{t}(X_{i})(Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}(X_{i}))(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i}))}{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}(t;x^{\mathtt{C}})}\lambda_{t}(X_{i})(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widetilde{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i}))^{2}},\quad\mathcal{I}_{1}(t;x^{\mathtt{C}})=\{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}:T_{i}=t,X_{i}^{\mathtt{C}}=x^{\mathtt{C}}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the LLN and Assumptions 1-2,
<math id="as1_S1.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})=\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})+O_{p}(n^{-1/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})=\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})+O_{p}(n^{-1/2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, under Assumption 4 the difference between <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, since their numerators and denominators differ only by replacing <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t},\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t},\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> with their oracle counterparts, and we have assumed implicitly that the denominators are bounded away from <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence
<math id="as1_S1.SS4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})=\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})+o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚁</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝙲</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{R}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})=\omega_{t,\mathtt{R}}(x^{\mathtt{C}})+o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
It follows by Cauchy-Schwarz that <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}=o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}=o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the fourth term in (<a href="#as1_S1.E1" title="In Proof. ‣ 1.4 Proof of Corollary 1 ‣ 1 Proofs ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) is handled similarly.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, all four terms vanish at <math id="as1_S1.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> rate, which proves the lemma.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Analogous to the proof of Theorem 1, Lemmas 3 and 4 together yield the proof of Corollary 1.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="as1_S1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.5 </span>Proof of Theorem 2</h3>

<div id="as1_S1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the proof of Theorem 2 from the main paper. Before delving into the theoretical analysis, we revisit the definitions and notations introduced in Section 4.2 to clarify the setup. Recall that the few-shot prediction generated by the LLM can be viewed as a function of the demonstrative subset <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, the query covariates <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Z)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the query treatment <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t,S)</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, the subset <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\left(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\left(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is an ordered collection of observations drawn i.i.d. from the unknown distribution <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> (Assumption 2). By design, the demonstrative subset <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and the query covariates (<math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Z</annotation></semantics></math>) are sampled from disjoint data folds (Steps <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> ), and are therefore independent. To account for the randomness in the demonstrative set, we have defined the expected few-shot prediction as <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((x,z),t)=\mathbb{E}_{S}[f_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t,S)\mid(X,Z)=(x,z)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((x,z),t)=\mathbb{E}_{S}[f_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t,S)\mid(X,Z)=(x,z)]</annotation></semantics></math> as the expected few-shot prediction after averaging over the randomness of the demonstrative subset <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, and the corresponding functions related to the LLM-based prediction have been defined as:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu^{\dagger}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu^{\dagger}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left(\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t)\mid X=x\right),\quad\omega^{\dagger}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(x)=\frac{\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}\left(Y,\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t)\mid X=x\right)}{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\left(\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t)\mid X=x\right)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left(\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t)\mid X=x\right),\quad\omega^{\dagger}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(x)=\frac{\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}\left(Y,\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t)\mid X=x\right)}{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\left(\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t)\mid X=x\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">by replacing the zero-shot prediction <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\dagger}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\dagger}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Following a similar two-part strategy as in the proof of Theorem 1, we first establish the asymptotic properties of the <span id="as1_S1.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">oracle</span> version of the CALM estimator under the few-shot setting. This oracle estimator is defined using the expected few-shot prediction <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t)</annotation></semantics></math>, along with the true nuisance functions <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\dagger}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\dagger}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{\dagger}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{\dagger}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\varphi_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\varphi_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varphi_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t))=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varphi_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t))=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}Y_{i}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}+\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}Y_{i}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}+\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\bigg(\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)+\omega_{t,\mathtt{FS}}\left(X_{i}\right)\left(\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t)-\mu_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\bigg(\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)+\omega_{t,\mathtt{FS}}\left(X_{i}\right)\left(\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t)-\mu_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Analogous to Lemma 1, we now state a corresponding result for the oracle version of the CALM estimator under the few-shot setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="as1_Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="as1_Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Asymptotic properties of the oracle CALM estimator, under the few-shot setting)<span id="as1_Thmlemma5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions 1-2, the oracle version of the CALM estimator under the few-shot setting is a consistent and asymptotically normal estimator of <math id="as1_Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, we have <math id="as1_Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}\xrightarrow{p}\mu_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}\xrightarrow{p}\mu_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{n}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}-\mu_{t}\right)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}\left(0,\mathsf{V}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{n}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}-\mu_{t}\right)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}\left(0,\mathsf{V}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_Thmlemma5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the asymptotic variance is given by:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t}\right)^{2}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)}{e_{t}(X)}\left(1-(1-e_{t}(X))\rho_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{2}(X)\right)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t}\right)^{2}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)}{e_{t}(X)}\left(1-(1-e_{t}(X))\rho_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{2}(X)\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_Thmlemma5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <math id="as1_Thmlemma5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(x)=\mathbb{C}\mathrm{orr}(Y(t),\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t))\mid X=x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">𝑂𝑃𝐸𝑁</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>orr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t,\mathtt{FS}}(x)=\mathbb{C}\mathrm{orr}(Y(t),\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t))\mid X=x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Recall from the proof of Theorem 1 that the zero-shot prediction <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\dagger}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\dagger}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}((X,Z),t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}((X,Z),t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Comparing Lemma 1 and Lemma 5, the only difference lies in replacing the zero-shot prediction <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}((X,Z),t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}((X,Z),t)</annotation></semantics></math> with the expected few-shot prediction <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X,Z),t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the proof of Lemma 5 follows exactly the same steps as in Lemma 1 and is omitted for brevity.</p>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In the second part of the proof, we show that, under the construction of the robust few-shot counterfactual predictions in Step 2<sup id="as1_S1.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="as1_S1.SS5.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">′</span></sup> and under Assumption 5, the difference between the constructed estimator and its oracle counterpart in the few-shot setting is asymptotically negligible. In contrast to the proof of Theorem 1, the proof of Theorem 2 must account not only for the estimation error from cross-fitted nuisance functions, but also for the approximation error arising from estimating the expected few-shot prediction <math id="as1_S1.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((x,z),t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((x,z),t)</annotation></semantics></math> via the resampling-and-aggregation strategy. We state the following lemma:</p>
</div>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="as1_Thmlemma6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span><span id="as1_Thmlemma6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Asymptotic equivalence to oracle)<span id="as1_Thmlemma6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_Thmlemma6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions 1–2 and 5, the proposed CALM estimator under the few-shot setting <math id="as1_Thmlemma6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Section 2.2) is asymptotically equivalent to the oracle CALM estimator under the few-shot setting <math id="as1_Thmlemma6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}</annotation></semantics></math>, in the sense that</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}\big)=o_{p}(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{FS},\mathtt{Oracle}}\big)=o_{p}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Lemmas 3 and 4 together complete the proof of Theorem 2.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="as1_S1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.6 </span>Proof of Lemma 6</h3>

<div id="as1_S1.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="as1_S1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">By random sample splitting (Step 1<sup id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">′</span></sup>), it suffices to consider <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k_{1},k_{2},k_{3})=(1,2,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k_{1},k_{2},k_{3})=(1,2,3)</annotation></semantics></math>, and show that:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{n}(\widehat{\mu}^{\mathcal{I}_{3}}_{t,\texttt{CALM,FS}}-\widehat{\mu}^{\mathcal{I}_{3}}_{t,\texttt{CALM,FS,Oracle}})=o_{p}(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CALM,FS</mtext></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CALM,FS,Oracle</mtext></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{n}(\widehat{\mu}^{\mathcal{I}_{3}}_{t,\texttt{CALM,FS}}-\widehat{\mu}^{\mathcal{I}_{3}}_{t,\texttt{CALM,FS,Oracle}})=o_{p}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">We decompose the difference as:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="as1_S1.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{n}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}^{\mathcal{I}_{3}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}^{\mathcal{I}_{3}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{n}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM}}^{\mathcal{I}_{3}}-\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}^{\mathcal{I}_{3}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.E2X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{n}}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{3}\right|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{3}}\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)\Bigg\{\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{n}}{\left|\mathcal{I}_{3}\right|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{3}}\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)\Bigg\{\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="6" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="as1_S1.E2Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.E2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\omega_{t,\mathtt{FS}}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\left(\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t)-\mu_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\omega_{t,\mathtt{FS}}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\left(\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t)-\mu_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="as1_S1.E2Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.E2Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left(Y^{\dagger}_{i,\mathtt{FS}}(t;\mathcal{I}_{1})-\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t)\right)\omega_{t,\mathtt{FS}}\left(X_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left(Y^{\dagger}_{i,\mathtt{FS}}(t;\mathcal{I}_{1})-\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t)\right)\omega_{t,\mathtt{FS}}\left(X_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="as1_S1.E2Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.E2Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left(Y^{\dagger}_{i,\mathtt{FS}}(t;\mathcal{I}_{1})-\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t)\right)\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\omega_{t,\mathtt{FS}}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left(Y^{\dagger}_{i,\mathtt{FS}}(t;\mathcal{I}_{1})-\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t)\right)\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\omega_{t,\mathtt{FS}}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="as1_S1.E2Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.E2Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\dagger\mathcal{I}_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\omega_{t,\mathtt{FS}}\left(X_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">†</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\dagger\mathcal{I}_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\omega_{t,\mathtt{FS}}\left(X_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="as1_S1.E2Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.E2Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\dagger\mathcal{I}_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\omega_{t,\mathtt{FS}}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">†</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\dagger\mathcal{I}_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\mu_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t,\mathtt{FS}}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}\left(X_{i}\right)-\omega_{t,\mathtt{FS}}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">To bound the remaining term, it suffices to show that for each <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{I}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{I}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\dagger}_{i,\mathtt{FS}}(t;\mathcal{I}_{1})-\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t)=o_{p}(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\dagger}_{i,\mathtt{FS}}(t;\mathcal{I}_{1})-\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((X_{i},Z_{i}),t)=o_{p}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\dagger}_{i,\mathtt{FS}}(t;\mathcal{I}_{1})=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}f_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}\big((X_{i},Z_{i}),t,\mathcal{S}_{b}^{\dagger}(\mathcal{I}_{1})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\dagger}_{i,\mathtt{FS}}(t;\mathcal{I}_{1})=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}f_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}\big((X_{i},Z_{i}),t,\mathcal{S}_{b}^{\dagger}(\mathcal{I}_{1})\big)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\notin\mathcal{I}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\notin\mathcal{I}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, it suffices to show that as <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, for each fixed <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,z)</annotation></semantics></math> in the support of <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Z)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}f_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}\big((x,z),t,\mathcal{S}_{b}^{\dagger}(\mathcal{I}_{1})\big)-\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((x,z),t)=o_{p}(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}f_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}\big((x,z),t,\mathcal{S}_{b}^{\dagger}(\mathcal{I}_{1})\big)-\bar{f}_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}((x,z),t)=o_{p}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">To simplify notation, we temporarily omit the fixed <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,z)</annotation></semantics></math> and the treatment <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and focus solely on the randomness induced by demonstrative subset sampling. Let <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> denote an ordered subset of size <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, drawn without replacement from the data in <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the function <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m}):=f_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}\big((x,z),t,(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙵𝚂</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m}):=f_{\theta,\mathtt{FS}}\big((x,z),t,(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is deterministic but potentially asymmetric (i.e., order-sensitive) in its arguments. Let each resampled subset <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{b}^{\dagger}(\mathcal{I}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{b}^{\dagger}(\mathcal{I}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> be expressed as <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(O_{1,b},\ldots,O_{m,b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(O_{1,b},\ldots,O_{m,b})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, Equation (<a href="#as1_S1.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ 1.6 Proof of Lemma 6 ‣ 1 Proofs ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) can be rewritten as:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}g(O_{1,b},\ldots,O_{m,b})-\mathbb{E}[g(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})]=o_{p}(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}g(O_{1,b},\ldots,O_{m,b})-\mathbb{E}[g(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})]=o_{p}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">To prove this, we invoke one-sample U-statistics theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#as1_bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#as1_bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>. Define the U-statistic of order <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> with asymmetric kernel as:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{n_{1}}(g):=\frac{1}{\prod_{i=0}^{m-1}(n_{1}-i)}\sum_{(\mathcal{I}_{1},\ldots,i_{m})\in J_{m,n_{1}}}g(O_{\mathcal{I}_{1}},\ldots,O_{i_{m}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{n_{1}}(g):=\frac{1}{\prod_{i=0}^{m-1}(n_{1}-i)}\sum_{(\mathcal{I}_{1},\ldots,i_{m})\in J_{m,n_{1}}}g(O_{\mathcal{I}_{1}},\ldots,O_{i_{m}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}=|\mathcal{I}_{1}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}=|\mathcal{I}_{1}|</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{m,n_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{m,n_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-tuples from <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with distinct entries. We decompose the difference as follows:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex44X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex44X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}g(O_{1,b},\ldots,O_{m,b})-\mathbb{E}[g(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}g(O_{1,b},\ldots,O_{m,b})-\mathbb{E}[g(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex44Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex44Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\big(\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}g(O_{1,b},\ldots,O_{m,b})-U_{n_{1}}(g)\big)}_{\text{(I)}}+\underbrace{\left(U_{n_{1}}(g)-\mathbb{E}[g(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})]\right)}_{\text{(II)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>(I)</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>(II)</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\big(\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}g(O_{1,b},\ldots,O_{m,b})-U_{n_{1}}(g)\big)}_{\text{(I)}}+\underbrace{\left(U_{n_{1}}(g)-\mathbb{E}[g(O_{1},\ldots,O_{m})]\right)}_{\text{(II)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex44Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex44Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=o_{p}(1)+O_{p}(n_{1}^{-1/2})=o_{p}(1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=o_{p}(1)+O_{p}(n_{1}^{-1/2})=o_{p}(1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text">where (I) is the re-sampling error that vanishes as <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second term (II) can be bounded by employing standard U-statistic convergence rate <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m24" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O_{p}(n_{1}^{-1/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{p}(n_{1}^{-1/2})</annotation></semantics></math> for fixed <math id="as1_S1.SS6.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#as1_bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>. This verifies Equation (<a href="#as1_S1.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ 1.6 Proof of Lemma 6 ‣ 1 Proofs ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). To complete the proof of Lemma 6, we can simply apply Assumption 5 and follow analogous arguments as used in the proof of Lemma 2 to verify Equation (<a href="#as1_S1.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ 1.6 Proof of Lemma 6 ‣ 1 Proofs ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="as1_S1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.7 </span>Proof of Corollary 2</h3>

<div id="as1_S1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now provide the proof of Corollary 2 from the main paper. Analogous to the proof of Lemma 2 in Section 1.3, it can be shown that under the assumptions of Corollary 2, the effect of estimated nuisance functions
<math id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{\ell}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{\ell}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t^{\prime}}^{\mathcal{I}_{\ell}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t^{\prime}}^{\mathcal{I}_{\ell}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger,\mathcal{I}_{\ell}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">†</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger,\mathcal{I}_{\ell}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t^{\prime}}^{\dagger,\mathcal{I}_{\ell}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo rspace="0em">†</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t^{\prime}}^{\dagger,\mathcal{I}_{\ell}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\omega}}_{\texttt{ATE}}^{\mathcal{I}_{\ell}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ATE</mtext><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\omega}}_{\texttt{ATE}}^{\mathcal{I}_{\ell}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>
on the asymptotics of the CALM estimator for the ATE,
<math id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is of higher order and negligible.
Hence, to prove Corollary 2 it suffices to study the asymptotic properties of the oracle CALM estimator with true nuisance functions
<math id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t^{\prime}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t^{\prime}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t^{\prime}}^{\dagger}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t^{\prime}}^{\dagger}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\omega}_{\texttt{ATE}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝎</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ATE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\omega}_{\texttt{ATE}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{oracle}}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\varphi_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\texttt{ATE}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))-\varphi_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\texttt{ATE}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t^{\prime}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚘𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{oracle}}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\varphi_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\texttt{ATE}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))-\varphi_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\texttt{ATE}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varphi_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\texttt{ATE}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varphi_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\texttt{ATE}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}Y_{i}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}+\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)\bigg(\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)+\omega_{t,\texttt{ATE}}\left(X_{i}\right)\left(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}Y_{i}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}+\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)}\right)\bigg(\mu_{t}\left(X_{i}\right)+\omega_{t,\texttt{ATE}}\left(X_{i}\right)\left(Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}\left(X_{i}\right)\right)\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The consistency and asymptotic normality of
<math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{oracle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚘𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{oracle}}</annotation></semantics></math>
follow directly from the proof of Lemma 1 (Section 1.2).
The main challenge is the computation of its asymptotic variance, which is more complicated than in Theorem 1 because of the correlation between the influence functions for the two arms.
Specifically, the asymptotic variance is:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Big[(\varphi_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\texttt{ATE}}-\varphi_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\texttt{ATE}}-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}})^{2}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Big[(\varphi_{t,\mathtt{CALM},\texttt{ATE}}-\varphi_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\texttt{ATE}}-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}})^{2}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigg\{\bigg[\mu_{t}(X)+\mu_{t^{\prime}}(X)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}+\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\big(Y-\mu_{t}(X)\big)+\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\Big)\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\big(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(X)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigg\{\bigg[\mu_{t}(X)+\mu_{t^{\prime}}(X)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}+\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\big(Y-\mu_{t}(X)\big)+\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\Big)\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\big(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(X)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t^{\prime}\}}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\big(Y-\mu_{t^{\prime}}(X)\big)-\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t^{\prime}\}}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\Big)\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\big(Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})-\mu_{t^{\prime}}^{\dagger}(X)\big)\bigg]^{2}\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t^{\prime}\}}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\big(Y-\mu_{t^{\prime}}(X)\big)-\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t^{\prime}\}}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\Big)\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\big(Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})-\mu_{t^{\prime}}^{\dagger}(X)\big)\bigg]^{2}\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This can be decomposed as</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\big[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t^{\prime}}(X)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}})^{2}\big]+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\!\big[\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))^{2}\big]}_{\text{(I)}}+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\!\big[\Delta_{t^{\prime}}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime}))^{2}\big]}_{\text{(II)}}-2\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\!\big[\Delta_{t}\Delta_{t^{\prime}}\big]}_{\text{(III)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>(I)</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>(II)</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>(III)</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\big[(\mu_{t}(X)-\mu_{t^{\prime}}(X)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}})^{2}\big]+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\!\big[\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))^{2}\big]}_{\text{(I)}}+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\!\big[\Delta_{t^{\prime}}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime}))^{2}\big]}_{\text{(II)}}-2\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\!\big[\Delta_{t}\Delta_{t^{\prime}}\big]}_{\text{(III)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{t}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\big(Y-\mu_{t}(X)\big)+\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\Big)\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\big(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(X)\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\big(Y-\mu_{t}(X)\big)+\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t\}}{e_{t}(X)}\Big)\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\big(Y^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(X)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{t^{\prime}}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{t^{\prime}}(X,T,Y,Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t^{\prime}\}}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\big(Y-\mu_{t^{\prime}}(X)\big)+\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t^{\prime}\}}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\Big)\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\big(Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})-\mu_{t^{\prime}}^{\dagger}(X)\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t^{\prime}\}}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\big(Y-\mu_{t^{\prime}}(X)\big)+\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T=t^{\prime}\}}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\Big)\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\big(Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})-\mu_{t^{\prime}}^{\dagger}(X)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.4" class="ltx_p">After standard calculation, we have:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex53X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex53X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(I)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext>(I)</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(I)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex53X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\frac{1}{e_{t}(X)}\,\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)+\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}\,\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}^{2}(X)\,\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>ar</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>ar</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\frac{1}{e_{t}(X)}\,\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)+\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}\,\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}^{2}(X)\,\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex53Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex53Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\;2\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}\,\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\,\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(Y(t),Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X)\Bigg]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn> 2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>ov</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\;2\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}\,\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\,\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(Y(t),Y^{\dagger}(t)\mid X)\Bigg],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex53Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex53Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(II)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext>(II)</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(II)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex53Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\frac{1}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\,\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t^{\prime})\mid X)+\frac{1-e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\,\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}^{2}(X)\,\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})\mid X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>ar</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>ar</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\frac{1}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\,\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t^{\prime})\mid X)+\frac{1-e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\,\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}^{2}(X)\,\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})\mid X)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex53Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex53Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\;2\frac{1-e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\,\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\,\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(Y(t^{\prime}),Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})\mid X)\Bigg]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn> 2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>ov</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\;2\frac{1-e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}\,\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\,\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(Y(t^{\prime}),Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})\mid X)\Bigg],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex53Xd"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex53Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(III)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext>(III)</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(III)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex53Xd.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Big[\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\,\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime}),Y(t)\mid X)+\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\,\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(Y^{\dagger}(t),Y(t^{\prime})\mid X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>ov</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>ov</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Big[\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\,\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime}),Y(t)\mid X)+\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\,\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(Y^{\dagger}(t),Y(t^{\prime})\mid X)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex53Xe"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex53Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\;\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\,\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\,\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(Y^{\dagger}(t),Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})\mid X)\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>ov</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\;\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\,\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}(X)\,\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(Y^{\dagger}(t),Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})\mid X)\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Summing over the terms (I)–(III) and rearranging terms yield:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex54X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex54X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex54X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\bigg\{(\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(X)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}})^{2}+\operatorname{Var}(Y(t)-Y(t^{\prime})\mid X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\bigg\{(\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(X)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}})^{2}+\operatorname{Var}(Y(t)-Y(t^{\prime})\mid X)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex54Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex54Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\left[\left.\sqrt{\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}}\left(Y(t)-\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}(X)Y^{\dagger}(t)\right)+\sqrt{\frac{1-e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}}\left(Y(t^{\prime})-\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}(X)Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})\right)\right\rvert\,X\right]\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>ar</mi><mo>[</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\left[\left.\sqrt{\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}}\left(Y(t)-\omega_{t,\mathtt{ATE}}(X)Y^{\dagger}(t)\right)+\sqrt{\frac{1-e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}}\left(Y(t^{\prime})-\omega_{t^{\prime},\mathtt{ATE}}(X)Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})\right)\right\rvert\,X\right]\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.6" class="ltx_p">To minimize <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\omega}_{\mathtt{ATE}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝎</mi><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\omega}_{\mathtt{ATE}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\big(\sqrt{\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}}Y^{\dagger}(t),\sqrt{\frac{1-e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}}Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})\big)^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\big(\sqrt{\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}}Y^{\dagger}(t),\sqrt{\frac{1-e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}}Y^{\dagger}(t^{\prime})\big)^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\sqrt{\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}}Y(t)+\sqrt{\frac{1-e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}}Y(t^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\sqrt{\frac{1-e_{t}(X)}{e_{t}(X)}}Y(t)+\sqrt{\frac{1-e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}}Y(t^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can rewrite <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\bigg\{(\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(X)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}})^{2}+\operatorname{Var}(Y(t)-Y(t^{\prime})\mid X)+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\big(Z-\bm{\omega}_{\mathtt{ATE}}(X)^{\prime}V\mid X\big)\bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝎</mi><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\bigg\{(\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(X)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}})^{2}+\operatorname{Var}(Y(t)-Y(t^{\prime})\mid X)+\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\big(Z-\bm{\omega}_{\mathtt{ATE}}(X)^{\prime}V\mid X\big)\bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.7" class="ltx_p">Under the assumption that <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{V}(x)\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{V}(x)\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimizer <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\omega}_{\mathtt{ATE}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝎</mi><mi>𝙰𝚃𝙴</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\omega}_{\mathtt{ATE}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{V}^{-1}(X)\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{V}^{-1}(X)\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{V}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{V}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> is the conditional variance of <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X)</annotation></semantics></math> is the conditional covariance of <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="as1_S1.SS7.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, the asymptotic variance is given by:</p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Big[(\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(X)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}})^{2}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)}{e_{t}(X)}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t^{\prime})\mid X)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}-\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X)^{\prime}\Sigma_{V}^{-1}(X)\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X)\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Big[(\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(X)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}})^{2}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X)}{e_{t}(X)}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t^{\prime})\mid X)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(X)}-\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X)^{\prime}\Sigma_{V}^{-1}(X)\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X)\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="as1_S1.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.8 </span>Proof of Corollary 3</h3>

<div id="as1_S1.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the proof of Corollary 3 from the main paper. Similar to the proof of Corollary 2, we start by defining the oracle version of the CALM-based CATE estimator as</p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)=\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})\left\{\varphi_{t,\texttt{CALM,ATE}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))-\varphi_{t^{\prime},\texttt{CALM,ATE}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t^{\prime}))\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CALM,ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CALM,ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)=\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})\left\{\varphi_{t,\texttt{CALM,ATE}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))-\varphi_{t^{\prime},\texttt{CALM,ATE}}(Y_{i},T_{i},X_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t^{\prime}))\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the linear smoother weights <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math> are kernel weights <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{K\!\left(\frac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}K\!\left(\frac{X_{j}-x}{h}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.801em;" width="0.801em"><mi>K</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.801em;" width="0.801em"><mi>K</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{K\!\left(\frac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}K\!\left(\frac{X_{j}-x}{h}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> with bandwidth <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, and the influence functions <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{t,\texttt{CALM,ATE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CALM,ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{t,\texttt{CALM,ATE}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{t^{\prime},\texttt{CALM,ATE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CALM,ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{t^{\prime},\texttt{CALM,ATE}}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined in Section 1.7 of the Supplementary Materials.</p>
</div>
<div id="as1_Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="as1_Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption S.1</span></span><span id="as1_Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Regularity conditions for kernel regression estimator of CATE)<span id="as1_Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="as1_Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="as1_S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="as1_S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="as1_S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Smoothness)</span><span id="as1_S1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> The conditional effect </span><math id="as1_S1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="as1_S1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> has bounded continuous second derivatives in a neighborhood of </span><math id="as1_S1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="as1_S1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="as1_S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="as1_S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Kernel)</span><span id="as1_S1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="as1_S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:\mathbb{R}^{p}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:\mathbb{R}^{p}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="as1_S1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a bounded, symmetric kernel of order two, i.e.</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int K(u)du=1,\quad\int uK(u)du=0,\quad\int uu^{\top}K(u)du=\mu_{2}(K)I_{p},\quad 0&lt;\mu_{2}(K)&lt;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int K(u)du=1,\quad\int uK(u)du=0,\quad\int uu^{\top}K(u)du=\mu_{2}(K)I_{p},\quad 0&lt;\mu_{2}(K)&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="as1_S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="as1_S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Bandwidth)</span><span id="as1_S1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> The bandwidth </span><math id="as1_S1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math><span id="as1_S1.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfies </span><math id="as1_S1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\to 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="as1_S1.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="as1_S1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nh^{p}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nh^{p}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="as1_S1.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and </span><math id="as1_S1.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nh^{p+4}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nh^{p+4}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="as1_S1.I1.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="as1_S1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="as1_S1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Covariate distribution)</span><span id="as1_S1.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> The density </span><math id="as1_S1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{X}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{X}(x)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="as1_S1.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is continuous and bounded away from </span><math id="as1_S1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="as1_S1.I1.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="as1_S1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="as1_S1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Moments)</span><span id="as1_S1.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="as1_S1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(\varphi_{t,\texttt{CALM,ATE}}-\varphi_{t^{\prime},\texttt{CALM,ATE}})^{2}\mid X=x]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CALM,ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CALM,ATE</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(\varphi_{t,\texttt{CALM,ATE}}-\varphi_{t^{\prime},\texttt{CALM,ATE}})^{2}\mid X=x]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="as1_S1.I1.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Leveraging the standard theory of kernel regression estimators, we state the following result:</p>
</div>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="as1_Thmlemma7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7</span></span><span id="as1_Thmlemma7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_Thmlemma7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions 1–2 and <a href="#as1_Thmassumption1" title="Assumption S.1 (Regularity conditions for kernel regression estimator of CATE). ‣ 1.8 Proof of Corollary 3 ‣ 1 Proofs ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S.1</span></a>, for any fixed <math id="as1_Thmlemma7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="as1_Thmlemma7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)\xrightarrow{p}\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)\xrightarrow{p}\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>,
and</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{nh^{p}}\,\Big(\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)\Big)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{\|K\|_{2}^{2}\,\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)}{f_{X}(x)}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{nh^{p}}\,\Big(\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)\Big)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\frac{\|K\|_{2}^{2}\,\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)}{f_{X}(x)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_Thmlemma7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="as1_Thmlemma7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|K\|_{2}^{2}=\int K(u)^{2}du" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|K\|_{2}^{2}=\int K(u)^{2}du</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)=\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X=x)}{e_{t}(x)}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t^{\prime})\mid X=x)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(x)}-\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X=x)^{\top}\Sigma_{V}^{-1}(x)\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X=x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)=\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X=x)}{e_{t}(x)}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t^{\prime})\mid X=x)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(x)}-\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X=x)^{\top}\Sigma_{V}^{-1}(x)\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X=x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="as1_S1.SS8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We provide only a short proof of this lemma, as most arguments follow directly from the standard theory of kernel regression estimators <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#as1_bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#as1_bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#as1_bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>. Under Assumptions 1-2 and <a href="#as1_Thmassumption1" title="Assumption S.1 (Regularity conditions for kernel regression estimator of CATE). ‣ 1.8 Proof of Corollary 3 ‣ 1 Proofs ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S.1</span></a>, a second-order Taylor expansion of <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> around <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> combined with the symmetry of the kernel shows that</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)]-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)=\tfrac{1}{2}h^{2}\mu_{2}(K)\,\Delta\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)+o(h^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)]-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)=\tfrac{1}{2}h^{2}\mu_{2}(K)\,\Delta\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)+o(h^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS8.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)=\sum_{j=1}^{p}\partial^{2}\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)/\partial x_{j}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)=\sum_{j=1}^{p}\partial^{2}\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)/\partial x_{j}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Laplacian of <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, define the conditional variance of the difference of influence functions as
<math id="as1_S1.SS8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)=\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t,\texttt{CALM,ATE}}-\varphi_{t^{\prime},\texttt{CALM,ATE}}\mid X=x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CALM,ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CALM,ATE</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)=\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(\varphi_{t,\texttt{CALM,ATE}}-\varphi_{t^{\prime},\texttt{CALM,ATE}}\mid X=x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Standard kernel variance expansion then gives</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\!\big(\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)\big)=\frac{1}{nh^{p}}\,\frac{\|K\|_{2}^{2}}{f_{X}(x)}\,\sigma^{2}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)+o\!\left(\frac{1}{nh^{p}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.838em;" width="0.838em"><mi>ar</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.315em;" width="0.315em"><mi>o</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}\!\big(\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)\big)=\frac{1}{nh^{p}}\,\frac{\|K\|_{2}^{2}}{f_{X}(x)}\,\sigma^{2}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)+o\!\left(\frac{1}{nh^{p}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS8.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the bias and variance expansions, we obtain the CLT:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{nh^{p}}\Big(\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)-\tfrac{1}{2}h^{2}\mu_{2}(K)\Delta\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)\Big)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\;\frac{\|K\|_{2}^{2}}{f_{X}(x)}\,\sigma^{2}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{nh^{p}}\Big(\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)-\tfrac{1}{2}h^{2}\mu_{2}(K)\Delta\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x)\Big)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\;\frac{\|K\|_{2}^{2}}{f_{X}(x)}\,\sigma^{2}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS8.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, adapting the asymptotic variance computation from the proof of Corollary 2, we have</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{2}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\big[(\varphi_{t,\texttt{CALM,ATE}}-\varphi_{t^{\prime},\texttt{CALM,ATE}}-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x))^{2}\mid X=x\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CALM,ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CALM,ATE</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\big[(\varphi_{t,\texttt{CALM,ATE}}-\varphi_{t^{\prime},\texttt{CALM,ATE}}-\tau_{t,t^{\prime}}(x))^{2}\mid X=x\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X=x)}{e_{t}(x)}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t^{\prime})\mid X=x)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(x)}-\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X=x)^{\top}\Sigma_{V}^{-1}(x)\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X=x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ar</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t)\mid X=x)}{e_{t}(x)}+\frac{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}(Y(t^{\prime})\mid X=x)}{e_{t^{\prime}}(x)}-\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X=x)^{\top}\Sigma_{V}^{-1}(x)\mathbb{C}\mathrm{ov}(V,Z\mid X=x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS8.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS8.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the bias is <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(h^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(h^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and the variance is <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O((nh^{p})^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O((nh^{p})^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, both vanish under the bandwidth conditions in Assumption <a href="#as1_Thmassumption1" title="Assumption S.1 (Regularity conditions for kernel regression estimator of CATE). ‣ 1.8 Proof of Corollary 3 ‣ 1 Proofs ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S.1</span></a>(3), ensuring consistency. To perform valid inference, one may employ undersmoothing so that <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{nh^{p}}\,h^{2}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{nh^{p}}\,h^{2}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which removes the asymptotic bias. This completes the proof of Lemma 7.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS8.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS8.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS8.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we show that the asymptotic difference between
<math id="as1_S1.SS8.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>
and the proposed CALM-based CATE estimator in Section 3.2 of the main paper
<math id="as1_S1.SS8.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>
is negligible in the kernel regression regime.</p>
</div>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="as1_Thmlemma8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8</span></span><span id="as1_Thmlemma8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="as1_Thmlemma8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_Thmlemma8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_Thmlemma8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the assumptions of Corollary 2 hold. Under Assumption <a href="#as1_Thmassumption1" title="Assumption S.1 (Regularity conditions for kernel regression estimator of CATE). ‣ 1.8 Proof of Corollary 3 ‣ 1 Proofs ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S.1</span></a>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{nh^{p}}\big(\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)-\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)\big)=o_{p}(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙲𝙰𝙻𝙼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙾𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{nh^{p}}\big(\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM}}(x)-\widehat{\tau}_{t,t^{\prime},\mathtt{CALM},\mathtt{Oracle}}(x)\big)=o_{p}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS8.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="as1_S1.SS8.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">By analogy to the proof of Lemma 2 in Section 1.3, and by symmetry between arms <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to show that the remainder term</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{3}=\sqrt{nh^{p}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}\right)\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{3}=\sqrt{nh^{p}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})\left(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}\right)\left(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{I_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">satisfies <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{3}=o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{3}=o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, where the kernel weights are <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})=\frac{K\!\left(\frac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}K\!\left(\frac{X_{j}-x}{h}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.801em;" width="0.801em"><mi>K</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.801em;" width="0.801em"><mi>K</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})=\frac{K\!\left(\frac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}K\!\left(\frac{X_{j}-x}{h}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Conditionally on <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and the observed structured covariates <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the variance of <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\Bigg(\sqrt{nh^{p}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}\Big)\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\big)\Bigg)^{2}\,\Big|\,\mathcal{I}_{2},\{X_{i}\}\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\Bigg(\sqrt{nh^{p}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})\Big(1-\frac{\bm{1}\{T_{i}=t\}}{e_{t}(X_{i})}\Big)\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\big)\Bigg)^{2}\,\Big|\,\mathcal{I}_{2},\{X_{i}\}\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=nh^{p}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})^{2}\,\frac{1-e_{t}(X_{i})}{e_{t}(X_{i})}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\big)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=nh^{p}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})^{2}\,\frac{1-e_{t}(X_{i})}{e_{t}(X_{i})}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\big)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\cdot nh^{p}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})^{2}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\big)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\cdot nh^{p}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}w_{i}(x;\mathbf{X})^{2}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\big)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C\cdot nh^{p}\cdot\frac{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}K\!\left(\tfrac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)^{2}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\big)^{2}}{\Big(\sum_{j=1}^{n}K\!\left(\frac{X_{j}-x}{h}\right)\Big)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.751em;" width="0.751em"><mi>K</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.751em;" width="0.751em"><mi>K</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C\cdot nh^{p}\cdot\frac{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}K\!\left(\tfrac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)^{2}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\big)^{2}}{\Big(\sum_{j=1}^{n}K\!\left(\frac{X_{j}-x}{h}\right)\Big)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C\cdot\frac{|\mathcal{I}_{1}|}{n}\cdot\frac{\tfrac{1}{|\mathcal{I}_{1}|h^{p}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}K\!\left(\frac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)^{2}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\big)^{2}}{\Big(\frac{1}{nh^{p}}\sum_{j=1}^{n}K\!\left(\frac{X_{j}-x}{h}\right)\Big)^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.751em;" width="0.751em"><mi>K</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.751em;" width="0.751em"><mi>K</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C\cdot\frac{|\mathcal{I}_{1}|}{n}\cdot\frac{\tfrac{1}{|\mathcal{I}_{1}|h^{p}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}K\!\left(\frac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)^{2}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\big)^{2}}{\Big(\frac{1}{nh^{p}}\sum_{j=1}^{n}K\!\left(\frac{X_{j}-x}{h}\right)\Big)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">For the denominator, by the LLN and Assumption <a href="#as1_Thmassumption1" title="Assumption S.1 (Regularity conditions for kernel regression estimator of CATE). ‣ 1.8 Proof of Corollary 3 ‣ 1 Proofs ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S.1</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="as1_S1.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="as1_S1.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{nh^{p}}\sum_{j=1}^{n}K\left(\frac{X_{j}-x}{h}\right)\xrightarrow{p}\frac{1}{h^{p}}\int K\left(\frac{u-x}{h}\right)f_{X}(u)du=f_{X}(x)&gt;0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{nh^{p}}\sum_{j=1}^{n}K\left(\frac{X_{j}-x}{h}\right)\xrightarrow{p}\frac{1}{h^{p}}\int K\left(\frac{u-x}{h}\right)f_{X}(u)du=f_{X}(x)&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the limit follows from a change of variables and <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int K(u)\,du=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int K(u)\,du=1</annotation></semantics></math>. For the numerator, since <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded with <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int K(u)^{2}du&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int K(u)^{2}du&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, by the dominated convergence theorem and Assumption 3 (<math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}-\mu_{t}\|_{L^{2}}=o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}-\mu_{t}\|_{L^{2}}=o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>), we obtain</span></p>
<table id="as1_S1.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S1.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{|\mathcal{I}_{1}|h^{p}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}K\!\left(\tfrac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)^{2}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\big)^{2}\xrightarrow{p}f_{X}(x)\int K(z)^{2}dz\cdot\mathbb{E}\!\big[(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X)-\mu_{t}(X))^{2}\big]=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.751em;" width="0.751em"><mi>K</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{|\mathcal{I}_{1}|h^{p}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{1}}K\!\left(\tfrac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)^{2}\big(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X_{i})-\mu_{t}(X_{i})\big)^{2}\xrightarrow{p}f_{X}(x)\int K(z)^{2}dz\cdot\mathbb{E}\!\big[(\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\mathcal{I}_{2}}(X)-\mu_{t}(X))^{2}\big]=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">By Slutsky’s theorem, the variance of <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is therefore <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. By Chebyshev’s inequality, <math id="as1_S1.SS8.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{3}=o_{p}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{3}=o_{p}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Analogous arguments apply to the other remainder terms as in Lemma 2, completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="as1_S1.SS8.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S1.SS8.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Combining Lemmas 7 and 8 establishes Corollary 3.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="as1_S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Test of efficiency improvement</h2>

<div id="as1_S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide additional details of the implementation of the efficiency improvement test described in Remark 1 of the main text, which assesses whether the conditional covariance <math id="as1_S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly zero, without delving into the full theoretical details. Let <math id="as1_S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{t}=\#\{i:T_{i}=t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{t}=\#\{i:T_{i}=t\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the number of subjects assigned to treatment <math id="as1_S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="as1_S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{X,t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{X,t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the conditional density of <math id="as1_S2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="as1_S2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=t</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="as1_S2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\gamma}_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\gamma}_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is estimated using a kernel estimator, standard arguments <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#as1_bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#as1_bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#as1_bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> yield the expansion:</p>
<table id="as1_S2.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sqrt{n_{t}h^{p}}\,\big(\widehat{\gamma}_{t}(x)-\gamma_{t}(x)\big)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{n_{t}h^{p}}}\sum_{i:T_{i}=t}\psi_{t}(x;X_{i},Y_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))+\text{Bias}_{t}(x)+R_{t}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>Bias</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n_{t}h^{p}}\,\big(\widehat{\gamma}_{t}(x)-\gamma_{t}(x)\big)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{n_{t}h^{p}}}\sum_{i:T_{i}=t}\psi_{t}(x;X_{i},Y_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))+\text{Bias}_{t}(x)+R_{t}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="as1_S2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Bias}_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>Bias</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Bias}_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the kernel smoothing bias, <math id="as1_S2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is a negligible remainder term, and:</p>
<table id="as1_S2.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t}(x;X_{i},Y_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))=\frac{1}{f_{X,t}(x)}\,K\!\left(\tfrac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)\big\{Y_{i}Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}(X_{i})Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})Y_{i}+\mu_{t}(X_{i})\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})-\gamma_{t}(X_{i})\big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.751em;" width="0.751em"><mi>K</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t}(x;X_{i},Y_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))=\frac{1}{f_{X,t}(x)}\,K\!\left(\tfrac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)\big\{Y_{i}Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}(X_{i})Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})Y_{i}+\mu_{t}(X_{i})\mu_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})-\gamma_{t}(X_{i})\big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">With a properly chosen bandwidth <math id="as1_S2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> and regularity conditions, both <math id="as1_S2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Bias}_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>Bias</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Bias}_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="as1_S2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> vanish uniformly in <math id="as1_S2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> at polynomial rates (see, for example, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#as1_bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#as1_bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#as1_bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>). Under <math id="as1_S2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="as1_S2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}(x)\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}(x)\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we replace <math id="as1_S2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by its plug-in estimate:</p>
<table id="as1_S2.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S2.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\psi}_{t}(x;X_{i},Y_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))=\frac{1}{\widehat{f}_{X,t}(x)}\,K\!\left(\tfrac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)\big\{Y_{i}Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widehat{\mu}_{t}(X_{i})Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})Y_{i}+\widehat{\mu}_{t}(X_{i})\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})\big\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.751em;" width="0.751em"><mi>K</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\psi}_{t}(x;X_{i},Y_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))=\frac{1}{\widehat{f}_{X,t}(x)}\,K\!\left(\tfrac{X_{i}-x}{h}\right)\big\{Y_{i}Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widehat{\mu}_{t}(X_{i})Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)-\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})Y_{i}+\widehat{\mu}_{t}(X_{i})\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}(X_{i})\big\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="as1_S2.p1.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{f}_{X,t}(x)=\frac{1}{n_{t}h^{p}}\sum_{i:T_{i}=t}K((X_{i}-x)/h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}_{X,t}(x)=\frac{1}{n_{t}h^{p}}\sum_{i:T_{i}=t}K((X_{i}-x)/h)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="as1_S2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{t},\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{t},\widehat{\mu}_{t}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> are kernel estimators of <math id="as1_S2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t},\mu_{t}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t},\mu_{t}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The covariance kernel is then estimated by</p>
<table id="as1_S2.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S2.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}_{t}(x,x^{\prime})=\frac{1}{n_{t}h^{p}}\sum_{i:T_{i}=t}\widehat{\psi}_{t}(x;X_{i},Y_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))\,\widehat{\psi}_{t}(x^{\prime};X_{i},Y_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)),\qquad\widehat{\sigma}_{t}^{2}(x)=\widehat{\Sigma}_{t}(x,x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}_{t}(x,x^{\prime})=\frac{1}{n_{t}h^{p}}\sum_{i:T_{i}=t}\widehat{\psi}_{t}(x;X_{i},Y_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t))\,\widehat{\psi}_{t}(x^{\prime};X_{i},Y_{i},Y_{i}^{\dagger}(t)),\qquad\widehat{\sigma}_{t}^{2}(x)=\widehat{\Sigma}_{t}(x,x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and on a fine grid <math id="as1_S2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{1},\dots,x_{M}\}\subset\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{1},\dots,x_{M}\}\subset\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> (with <math id="as1_S2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> possibly increasing with <math id="as1_S2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>), we form the correlation matrix</p>
<table id="as1_S2.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S2.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{t}=(\widehat{\rho}_{t}(x_{j},x_{k}))_{j,k=1}^{M},\qquad\widehat{\rho}_{t}(x_{j},x_{k})=\frac{\widehat{\Sigma}_{t}(x_{j},x_{k})}{\widehat{\sigma}_{t}(x_{j})\widehat{\sigma}_{t}(x_{k})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{t}=(\widehat{\rho}_{t}(x_{j},x_{k}))_{j,k=1}^{M},\qquad\widehat{\rho}_{t}(x_{j},x_{k})=\frac{\widehat{\Sigma}_{t}(x_{j},x_{k})}{\widehat{\sigma}_{t}(x_{j})\widehat{\sigma}_{t}(x_{k})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">We then simulate Gaussian vectors <math id="as1_S2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\sim N(0,\widehat{R}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\sim N(0,\widehat{R}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> to approximate the distribution of <math id="as1_S2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{x}|G(x)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{x}|G(x)|</annotation></semantics></math>. The test statistic</p>
<table id="as1_S2.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="as1_S2.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\sup_{x\in\{x_{1},\dots,x_{M}\}}\left|\frac{\sqrt{n_{t}h^{p}}\,\widehat{\gamma}_{t}(x)}{\widehat{\sigma}_{t}(x)}\right|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\sup_{x\in\{x_{1},\dots,x_{M}\}}\left|\frac{\sqrt{n_{t}h^{p}}\,\widehat{\gamma}_{t}(x)}{\widehat{\sigma}_{t}(x)}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="as1_S2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">leads to rejection of <math id="as1_S2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="as1_S2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{n_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{n_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds the simulated <math id="as1_S2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> quantile. As an alternative, the distribution may also be approximated using the multiplier bootstrap <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#as1_bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="as1_S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Motivating real-world RCTs</h2>

<div id="as1_S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present five motivating RCTs that collect unstructured data such as survey responses, video, and audio recordings from participants. These trials span cancer, mental health, and dementia care, as summarized in Table <a href="#as1_S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3 Motivating real-world RCTs ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and demonstrate the broad applicability of our proposed methods in real-world settings.</p>
</div>
<figure id="as1_S3.T1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="as1_S3.T1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="as1_S3.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="as1_S3.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.65pt 5.0pt;"><span id="as1_S3.T1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top" style="width:102.4pt;">
<span id="as1_S3.T1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_align_left ltx_noindent">
<span id="as1_S3.T1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S3.T1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="as1_S3.T1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
<span id="as1_S3.T1.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_top">
<span id="as1_S3.T1.p1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="as1_S3.T1.p1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.65pt 5.0pt;"><span id="as1_S3.T1.p1.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Trial</span></span></span>
<span id="as1_S3.T1.p1.1.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="as1_S3.T1.p1.1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.65pt 5.0pt;"><span id="as1_S3.T1.p1.1.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Name</span></span></span>
</span></span><span id="as1_S3.T1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
</span></span></td>
<td id="as1_S3.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.65pt 5.0pt;">
<span id="as1_S3.T1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="as1_S3.T1.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="as1_S3.T1.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Brief Summary</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="as1_S3.T1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.65pt 5.0pt;"><span id="as1_S3.T1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="as1_S3.T1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_align_left ltx_noindent">
<span id="as1_S3.T1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="as1_S3.T1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="as1_S3.T1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
<span id="as1_S3.T1.p2.1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_top">
<span id="as1_S3.T1.p2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
