<div id="as1_S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="as1_S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In what follows, we provide an example of the zero-shot learning prompt in Figure <a href="#as1_S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4 Additional simulation study details ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the few-shot learning prompt in Figure <a href="#as1_S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4 Additional simulation study details ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, and example prompts under different prompt engineering techniques in Figure <a href="#as1_S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4 Additional simulation study details ‣ Supplementary Materials for “Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?” ‣ Can language models boost the power of randomized experiments without statistical bias?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
